# One line ending for the whole repository: LF, everywhere, for every text
# file. Pinned rather than left to each contributor's `core.autocrlf`,
# because that setting is per-machine and invisible in a diff — a file's
# committed bytes used to depend on who last touched it and from which OS.
# The symptom was a rewrite that edited 15 lines showing up as a 97-line
# diff, because the new lines arrived with a different ending than the
# file's existing ones.
#
# LF specifically because it is what `dart format` emits. The formatter
# writes most lines in this repository, so matching it means a formatted
# file and a committed file agree, and `dart format` never produces a
# phantom diff of its own.
#
# This also matters for CI: drift's generated file is committed and checked
# against a regeneration. Without a pinned ending, a Linux runner and a
# Windows checkout disagree byte-for-byte on a file whose content is
# identical, and that check fails for no real reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Flutter regenerates these from a template on every Windows build. The
# generator emits LF; pinning them here stops the generator and a CRLF
# checkout from fighting over the file on each build.
windows/flutter/generated_* text eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` already detects these, but naming them means a
# corrupt or truncated file is refused rather than silently normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
